# Lindos's own package repository (updates for the lindos-* packages).
#
# This is the ONE place the repository address and suites are written. It is a configuration
# file: a Lindos update can move the repository to another server by shipping a new version of
# it (dpkg asks before replacing a copy you edited), and nothing else has to change.
#
# "Enabled: no" until a real signing key and a real server exist (docs/RELEASING.md). The
# address below is a reserved, never-resolving placeholder name, so an image built today cannot
# talk to, or trust, anything. When the owner sets a real address they flip this to "yes" in the
# same commit that adds the real public key and its fingerprint; a build refuses to ship a
# switched-on source without them (build/tools/check-archive-keyring.sh).
Enabled: no
Types: deb
URIs: https://apt.lindos.invalid/stable/
Suites: ./
Signed-By: /usr/share/keyrings/lindos-archive-keyring.gpg
